# LEVEL 12 → 13 — DECOMPRESSING A MULTI-LAYER COMPRESSED FILE


## LEVEL GOAL
Reverse a hexdump and decompress a file that has been compressed multiple times using different formats.

## DESCRIPTION
`data.txt` is a hexdump of a file compressed repeatedly using gzip, bzip2, and tar in alternating layers. The task requires identifying each layer and extracting until plain text is reached. This level builds methodical problem-solving habits under ambiguity.

## APPROACH

**Step 1 — Create a working directory in /tmp**

```bash
cd /tmp
mktemp -d
cd /tmp/tmp.XXXXXXXX
cp ~/data.txt .
```

**Step 2 — Reverse the hexdump back to binary**

```bash
xxd -r data.txt > data
```

**Step 3 — Iteratively identify and extract**

Run `file` after every extraction step to determine the next format:

```bash
file data          # → gzip compressed data
mv data data.gz && gunzip data.gz

file data          # → bzip2 compressed data
mv data data.bz2 && bunzip2 data.bz2

file data          # → gzip compressed data
mv data data.gz && gunzip data.gz

file data          # → POSIX tar archive
mv data data.tar && tar -xf data.tar

file data5.bin     # → POSIX tar archive
mv data5.bin data5.tar && tar -xf data5.tar

file data6.bin     # → bzip2 compressed data
mv data6.bin data6.bz2 && bunzip2 data6.bz2

file data6         # → POSIX tar archive
mv data6 data6.tar && tar -xf data6.tar

file data8.bin     # → gzip compressed data
mv data8.bin data.gz && gunzip data.gz

file data          # → ASCII text
cat data           # → Password
```

## Commands Learned

Command          Purpose 

`xxd -r`         Reverse hexdump to binary 
`file`           Identify file type from content 
`gunzip`         Extract gzip archives 
`bunzip2`        Extract bzip2 archives 
`tar -xf`        Extract tar archives 
`mktemp -d`      Create a secure temporary directory 

